            "review_title": "Review at Le Rabelais Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Anh Amắn 🇻🇳\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12939 contributions\n1\nDelicious French cuisine in Da Lat, Vietnam\nJan 2018 • Couples\nWhen the summer months get very hot in Ho Chi Minh City, Da Lat in the mountains is the traditional escape destination, normally 10 degrees cooler than HCMc. Le Rabelais Restaurant is situated in the Dalat Palace Hotel, a lavish colonial residence surrounded by lovely gardens. The restaurant decor carries through with an opulent colonial feel, chandeliers and art work, and full silver service and pianist playing Erik Satie. The food was heavily French influenced with a matching wine list. Definitely in the 5 star range for Vietnam, & pretty special for a birthday or an anniversary.\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 19, 2018",
